-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Hunter: Trap Launcher
--
-- Hunter traps in 3.3.5a are placed two yards in front of the caster.
-- EffectImplicitTargetA = 47 (TARGET_DEST_CASTER_FRONT) resolves off the
-- caster's own position in Spell::SelectImplicitCasterDestTargets
-- (Spell.cpp:1660-1698), and RangeIndex = 1 is self-range.  For a solo fork
-- this is the worst piece of Hunter design left: every trap needs a walk into
-- melee, or a Distracting Shot pull, before the fight can start.
--
-- Cataclysm solved it with Trap Launcher (77769).  That cannot be reproduced
-- here: Trap Launcher works by SPELL_AURA_OVERRIDE_ACTIONBAR_SPELLS, aura
-- 332, and 3.3.5a stops at TOTAL_AURAS = 317.  Nor can a server-side buff
-- retrofit a ground reticle -- the client draws the reticle from the cast
-- spell's own Targets flag, before the cast packet is ever sent.  A toggle is
-- not implementable on this client.
--
-- What *is* implementable is what Blizzard themselves shipped in Wrath
-- Classic patch 3.4.3: a separate, directly castable ranged trap spell
-- (Trap Launcher: Explosive Trap, 425777).  This file generalises that to
-- all five trap families.
--
-- Shape, modelled exactly on Freezing Arrow (60192 -> 60202), which is the
-- one ranged trap WotLK already had and which works on AzerothCore with no
-- C++ at all:
--
--                   castable parent          triggered child
--   Effect1         32 TRIGGER_MISSILE       104/105/106 SUMMON_OBJECT_SLOTn
--   TargetA1        87 TARGET_DEST_DEST      87 TARGET_DEST_DEST
--   Targets         64 DEST_LOCATION         64
--   RangeIndex      5  (0-40 yd)             6  (0-100 yd)
--   Speed           45.0 (arrow flight)      0
--   DurationIndex   0                        9  (30 s trap)
--   Category        411 / 1250 / 1249        0
--
-- Spell::EffectSummonObject already honours a destination
-- (SpellEffects.cpp:4609-4615):
--
--     if (m_targets.HasDst())
--         destTarget->GetPosition(x, y, z);
--     else
--         m_caster->GetClosePoint(x, y, z, DEFAULT_WORLD_OBJECT_SIZE);
--
-- so no core change is needed.  The whole feature is DBC data plus a small
-- PlayerScript that grants the spells (HunterTrapLauncher.cpp).
--
-- Deliberate decisions:
--
--   * Base traps are NOT modified.  Melee placement stays instant and free,
--     playerbot hunters keep casting exactly what they cast today, and there
--     is no regression surface.
--
--   * Each launched variant reuses its base rank's GameObject and object
--     slot, so the trap that lands is byte-identical to the melee-placed
--     one and the two replace each other.  This is what makes the whole
--     Survival tree keep working, and it is worth being precise about why.
--
--     SPELLFAMILY_HUNTER flag 0x80 is carried by the trap *placement*
--     spells, and almost no trap talent targets it.  The talents key off
--     the effect spells the GameObject casts:
--
--         Trap Mastery       mask 0x18   Freezing Trap Effect, Frost Trap Aura
--         Survival Tactics   mask 0x11c  Feign Death + all trap effects
--         Point of No Escape mask 0x8    Freezing Trap Effect
--         Entrapment, T.N.T., Lock and Load
--                            mask 0      C++/proc on trap activation
--
--     Reusing the base GameObject therefore matters far more than any
--     field on these spells: the effect spells are the same rows, so every
--     one of those talents applies without knowing the launcher exists.
--     Minting new GameObjects -- as real Freezing Arrow did with 193771
--     and its own "Freezing Arrow Effect" -- would have silently dropped
--     the launched traps out of Trap Mastery and Point of No Escape.
--
--     Resourcefulness is the one talent that reads the placement spell,
--     via its mana-cost effect (mask 0xde, which does include 0x80).  The
--     launchers carry SpellFamilyName 9 and SpellFamilyFlags 0x80 from
--     Freezing Arrow, so that applies too.
--
--     Unrelated pre-existing bug, noted here because it looks like one of
--     ours and is not: Resourcefulness' *cooldown* effect uses mask
--     0x84000 (Serpent Sting, Aspect of the Monkey), which does not cover
--     traps at all, despite the tooltip promising it.  Identical in
--     dbc/base/Spell.dbc and in the built DBC, with no script overriding
--     it, so base and launched traps are affected the same way.
--
--   * Same resource cost as the base trap (ManaCostPercentage 3/2/9/19/9).
--     Ranged placement is quality of life, not a tradeoff.
--
--   * The child carries Category = 0.  TrinityCore #15794: 60192 and 60202
--     share category 411, so casting the parent puts the child on cooldown
--     and the trap silently never spawns.  The shared 30 s trap cooldown
--     lives on the parent alone, where Player::AddSpellAndCategoryCooldowns
--     (Player.cpp:11026-11045) propagates it across the category -- note
--     that loop also requires a matching SpellFamilyName, which holds here.
--
--   * Names are distinct ("Trap Launcher: Explosive Trap"), matching 425777.
--     Cataclysm's override spells shared the base trap's name and broke every
--     /cast macro; there is no reason to repeat that.
--
--   * EquippedItemClass is -1, not Freezing Arrow's 2.  A launched trap that
--     silently fails because a bow broke would be a mystery bug, and the base
--     traps have no weapon requirement.
--
--   * SpellVisual1 stays 12409 (Freezing Arrow's) on every family, so there
--     is clear "something was launched" feedback.  A per-family missile
--     visual would be nicer and is left as polish.
--
-- IDs: 200700-200718 castable, 200720-200738 triggered.
-- Generated by tools/gen_sql.py via a one-off driver; see the per-spell
-- override comments below for what was changed off each clone base.
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

